After the game we sit on the bench.
We drink water and take a break.
Timo and Lena talk about a tournament.
They played a tournament last week.
Then Lena looks at me.
"Why Berlin anyway, Maya?" she asks.
"And how did you find your job?"
I smile and begin my story.
"I saw the advertisement in October."
"I wrote an application straight away."
"Then I waited a very long time."
"I needed a lot of papers."
"I filled out forms."
"I made an appointment at the embassy."
That all took a lot of time.
"But in January I finally packed my suitcase."
Timo laughs and picks up his racket.
"Then we got lucky," he says.
